nd passes through the point $(-2,3)$. To find the equation of this line, we use point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 &= m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(3) &= 2(x-(-2)) \\\\ y-(3) &= 2 x + 4 \\\\ y &= 2 x + 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, write the equation in standard form with coprime integer coefficients and a positive $x$-coefficient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2 x + 7 \\\\ 2 x -y &= -7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first blank is $2 x -y$ and the second blank is $-7$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482708 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186175912.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482708 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "f306f06a-785e-5d4c-bd17-02ca8cc6dc42" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186486467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186486475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186486486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186486514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1045 "The Cartesian Coordinate System" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186486467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "2ee8e36f-d6f2-535a-b7e8-f2094eda05e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485790 #edb/ref 1080 "(-3,-6)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485790 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485790 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e2f253f-f36a-560f-9ec1-161de7ca2936" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485807 #edb/ref 1080 "All" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485807 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485807 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "17d8031f-5e2f-5683-84c6-7fe7232955e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186